on a sync's fast-forward (introduced without it in 6049b1b, fixed in e9ab747).
Base: 7474470 (agentfs-core unchanged since). git: the release in ci/git-release.
Re-record (crates/agentfs-model/VERIFYING.md, "A regression found on the engine")
in a scratch worktree with this applied. Give it fresh volumes, since --record
refuses a non-empty OUT: export MODEL_TARGET_VOLUME=mt-fixture MODEL_WORK_VOLUME=mw-fixture
  ci/model-docker.sh -- sh -c 'AGENTFS_MODEL_TRACE_DIR=/work/t cargo test --locked \
    -p agentfs-conformance --test replay \
    finding_51_a_sync_that_cannot_show_the_upstreams_commit_merges'
    # exits 101: the copy fails the scenario at call 15, which is the point
  ci/model-docker.sh -- cargo run --locked -p agentfs-conformance --bin phase1-replay -- \
    library /work/t --min-scenarios 0 --min-seeds 0 \
    --only finding_51_a_sync_that --record /work/out
    # exits 1: MISMATCH at call 15, as expected; the recording is still written
  ci/model-docker.sh -- sh -c 'cp /work/out/finding_51_a_sync_that*.trace \
    crates/agentfs-conformance/tests/regressions/finding-51-sync-fast-forward.trace'
